        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospitalisation of your patient, a 67-year-old female, admitted on 08/09/2004 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, and arterial blood gas analysis confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests and pulse oximetry were performed to monitor her condition. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy with good clinical response. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout her stay. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. She is discharged in a stable condition and I recommend close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
